# Call-site ledger of asciinema at 350d5e9d8b7cee1be5db4091815942c9d035e7dc.
# Hand-written from the source; judgements in asciinema.md.
#
# The scope rules A, B1-B5 and C are in macro-benchmark/README.md. The
# package supports Python 3.4 and later (CHANGELOG drops 3.3; no upper bound) (setup.py exits on Python 2).
# Values used below (asciinema.md, "Values"):
#   env: the env of Config, get_config_home, load and the commands is the
#     package default os.environ; os.environ.get is collections.abc.Mapping.get
#     (earlier rulings: anytree, argcomplete, pypinyin). A mapping that a
#     client passes (the tests pass dicts to Config) is opaque (B5).
#   streams: open_url returns sys.stdin or a text file of open()
#     (io.TextIOWrapper), or, for an http(s) URL, an encodings.utf_8.StreamReader
#     over the http.client.HTTPResponse of urlopen or the gzip.GzipFile around
#     it, or over the urllib.response.addinfourl of a redirect to an ftp URL.
#     StreamReader has no close: its __getattr__ gives the close of the
#     wrapped stream.
#   asciicasts: open_from_url.__enter__ returns a v2.Asciicast or a v1.Asciicast.
#   pty.record: the package passes it only the async_writer and the
#     async_notifier of recorder.record (B2); the tests pass a client writer.
#   async_worker.py: both sides of the optional import run (multiprocessing
#     Process and Queue, or threading.Thread and queue.Queue).

